 "notes": "Curve traced from Fig. 4 (HPlimit.pdf in the arXiv e-print), the 'DAMIC at SNOLAB' solid blue line: 90% C.L. upper limit on hidden-photon DM kinetic mixing kappa (= chi = epsilon) vs hidden-photon mass m_V. Coordinates recovered from the vector figure (path 203, first/topmost legend entry, the deepest curve = the paper's own best limit) with log-log axis calibration from tick marks (x: 10^0 eV at px 81.5, decade=370.6 px; y: 10^-11 at py 112.0, decade=86.8 px). Reported directly as kappa, no conversion needed. The paper assumes rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (isothermal Maxwellian, v_esc=544, v0=220 km/s); not rescaled per task card. Note the paper's headline title result is DM-electron scattering cross section (Fig. 3), which is not a canonical coupling plane; the hidden-photon kinetic-mixing limit (Fig. 4) is the reportable canonical result. Mass range ~1.3-30 eV matches abstract's 1.2-30 eV.",
